  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 234 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nLittle change in the overall pattern through Friday as the upper \nlevel flow remains a modified westerlies leading to mild and mostly \ndry conditions. The caveat being Thursday night and Friday morning \nas a few showers and storms could develop by another round of \nmoisture return with surface low pressure moving to the east and \nreturn flow commences. Upper low pressure will descend into the \nPacific Northwest this weekend leading to a gradual amplification of \nsouthwest flow into Iowa. This will lead to warmer temperatures this \nweekend, with more widespread 80s possible. A bit beyond the 7 day \nforecast and perhaps the next widespread weather potential for Iowa \narrives mid next week as the upper low shifts east into the Plains \nand may bring thunderstorms back to Iowa.",
